# Positions where the engine, not the reading, is the weak link.
#
# These are NOT checked by selftest.py: none of them has a right answer the
# script can assert. They are here to be run by hand after editing solve.py,
# with the expected shape of the output written next to each. A change that
# made any of them worse would otherwise show up nowhere -- selftest.py and
# epdcheck.py both count mates found, and not one of these is about that.
#
# Run: python3 scripts/solve.py --quick "<fen>"          for rows 3-7
#      python3 scripts/solve.py --quick --playout 60 --budget 60 "<fen>"
#                                                       for rows 1-2
#
8/p7/kpP5/qrp1b3/rpP2b2/pP2b3/P7/K7 w - - 0 1              ; fortress. Truth: draw. Expect a large minus, the 50-move probe collapsing to 0.00, and a playout that never resets the clock. With --line Kb1: the verdict must say 'an evaluation, not a proof', never 'the win is forced', and the playout must end on a claimable draw, not on the budget.
1K1k4/1P6/8/8/8/8/r7/2R5 w - - 0 1                         ; Lucena. Truth: won. Expect the probe to collapse exactly as above -- it is one-sided -- and the playout to reset the clock within about twenty plies (14, 18 and 19 in three runs at 0.3 s a move; self-play is not deterministic) and finish 1-0.
8/8/8/8/8/2k5/8/KBN5 w - - 0 1                             ; K+B+N vs K. Truth: mate in <=33. Expect about +2.6 at any depth, the tablebase URL, and the probe collapsing. Never a mate score.
8/8/p1p5/1p5p/1P5p/8/PPP2K1p/4R1rk w - - 0 1               ; Truth: mate in 10 (reproducible with MultiPV 3). Expect a headline near +2.7 and replies that are mated: the verdict line must say the position mates down those branches, never "the win is not forced".
8/2P5/8/8/3r4/8/2K5/k7 w - - 0 1                           ; Saavedra key position. Expect c8=R, mate in 7. Underpromotion: a mate in 7 reported as a mate in 10 means the ladder or the re-probe regressed.
n6N/pr4p1/2ppp1Bk/P4p1P/r5PK/p6R/2PPP2N/8 w - - 0 1        ; matetrack, published #8. Known miss: expect an evaluation, no mate, at every setting tried. Recorded so a future fix is recognised as one.
2rn4/5p2/n1p1P2b/8/3kP1Pp/1P1Np3/1Kp1P3/1bB2N1B w - - 0 1  ; matetrack, published #9. Known miss, as above.
8/1Np1nN2/r3p1p1/p1Q5/3pkb2/B1R2pnK/3p4/5B2 w - - 0 1      ; Kg4, mate in 4, and only with the ladder. --fast returns Bd3+ mate in 6: that is the flag working as documented, not a regression. With --quick it must be the mate in 4.
